      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Himalayan Mountain System"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Himalayan Mountain System consists of young fold mountains comprising the Himadri, Himachal, and Shiwalik ranges.",
        "Trans-Himalayan ranges include the Karakoram, Ladakh, Zaskar, and Kailash ranges north of the Great Himalayas.",
        "The Peninsular Mountain System includes the ancient Aravallis, Vindhyas, Satpuras, and the Ghats.",
        "Western Ghats and Eastern Ghats converge at the Nilgiri Hills in Southern India.",
        "Mountains act as climate barriers, sources of major rivers, and biodiversity hotspots crucial for India's ecology."
      ],
      "id": "9tsfn1e"
    },
